# BT-020: Closing the Section 5 Judge Gap in the `boardctl render` HTML Report

**Repository:** `coding-hermes/boardctl`
**Feature commit:** `ff72fcb2aa54faf60e72e63129ee485880d262d1`
**Fix commit:** `bd9f52a533d735b4e61c045bc1c4a8fe497aa472`
**Judge evidence:** `.gitreins/history/2026-09-12/1249e112/verdict.json` (FAIL) → `.gitreins/history/2026-09-12/b1a3e017/verdict.json` (PASS)
**Normative source:** `docs/specs/board-analytics-report.md` §2.4, §3.9, §5.1–5.7, §7.1

## 1. Symptom

All 10 explicit §7.1 acceptance criteria passed with hard evidence, yet GitReins Tier 2 returned:

```
INCOMPLETE — Section 5 has unimplemented requirements despite all 10 explicit 7.1 acceptance criteria passing.
```

Four concrete gaps in the required §5 UX section:

| # | Gap | Spec clause |
|---|-----|-------------|
| 1 | Status/priority composition view absent; not recomputed on fixtures toggle | §3.9, §5.5 |
| 2 | Expanded-event detail bypassed the JSON-string / base64 ladder | §2.4, §5.3 |
| 3 | Zero streaks rendered `0d` instead of `0 (no activity)` | §5.7 |
| 4 | Wholly unparseable JSONL treated as empty board + warnings, not an error-state card excluded from compare | §5.7 |

## 2. Root-cause analysis

**Proximate cause:** implementation and tests targeted the 10 numbered §7.1 end-to-end probes. The task criterion actually requires spec **sections 2, 3, 5, 6**. Section 5 adds normative UX behaviors outside those probes, and four shipped missing.

**Why each escaped the AC suite:**
1. **Counts panel** — §7.1 never names it; the payload already had `derived.status_counts`/`priority_counts`, so payload checks passed while the client never rendered them.
2. **Detail ladder** — §7.1 only checks `<script>`/image escaping; the Go ladder existed but the client `detailBody()` only handled `typeof v === "object"`.
3. **Zero-streak wording** — the synthetic streak AC only covers positive/live/ended values.
4. **Error state** — §2.7/§7.1 only test a *torn line among valid rows*; the stronger "not JSONL at all" case had no loader threshold.

**Process cause:** no requirement-to-test matrix for the full normative UX section. The durable fix is code + a matrix (§3) + contract tests asserting each UI/data path.

## 3. Requirement-to-test matrix

| Spec req | Behavior | Regression test (`internal/render`) |
|----------|----------|-------------------------------------|
| §3.9 / §5.2 | V11 status + priority composition renders | `TestTemplateHasCountsPanel` |
| §3.9 / §5.5 | Fixtures toggle recomputes counts | `TestTemplateHasCountsPanel` |
| §5.7 | Empty composition states | `TestTemplateHasCountsPanel` |
| §2.4 / §5.3 | Full client-side detail ladder | `TestTemplateHasDetailLadder` |
| §5.7 | Zero streak → `0 (no activity)` | `TestTemplateHasNoActivityStreakWording` |
| §5.7 | Error card + compare exclusion | `TestTemplateHasErrorStateBoardCard` |
| §5.7 / §6.2 | Error board ships with non-empty `Error` | `TestErrorBoardExcludedFromComparePayload` |
| §5.7 | Unparseable `tasks.jsonl` → error state | `TestUnparseableRequiredFileIsErrorState` |
| §5.7 | Unparseable `events.jsonl` → error state | `TestUnparseableEventsFileIsErrorState` |
| §2.7 | One torn row among valid rows stays a warning | `TestTornLineAmongValidRowsStaysWarning` |
| §2.2 / §5.7 | Empty/header-only stay valid empty boards | `TestEmptyAndHeaderOnlyBoardsRemainValid` |

## 4. Exact fix

Six files: `derive.go`, `load.go`, `report.go`, `template.go`, `derive_test.go`, `load_test.go` (patch = diff `ff72fcb..bd9f52a`, 446 insertions / 18 deletions).

### 4.1 Loader threshold (`internal/render/load.go`)

```go
type boardData struct {
	...
	warns    warningSink
	fatal    string // 5.7 error state: required file wholly unparseable ("" = valid board)
}
```

Count candidates vs. successful parses in the task and event scans (same pattern each):

```go
	taskCand, taskParsed := 0, 0
	firstTaskErrLine := 0
	var firstTaskErr error
	for i := firstTaskIdx; i < len(tasksLines); i++ {
		line := tasksLines[i]
		if len(bytes.TrimSpace(line)) == 0 {
			continue
		}
		taskCand++
		row, err := board.ParseRow(line)
		if err != nil {
			if firstTaskErr == nil {
				firstTaskErrLine, firstTaskErr = i+1, err
			}
			d.warns.tasks++
			d.warns.note("tasks.jsonl line %d: skipped malformed row (%v)", i+1, err)
			continue
		}
		taskParsed++
		...
	}
```

Threshold:

```go
	switch {
	case taskCand > 0 && taskParsed == 0:
		d.fatal = fmt.Sprintf("tasks.jsonl: all %d row(s) failed to parse (first error, line %d: %v)", taskCand, firstTaskErrLine, firstTaskErr)
	case eventCand > 0 && eventParsed == 0:
		d.fatal = fmt.Sprintf("events.jsonl: all %d row(s) failed to parse (first error, line %d: %v)", eventCand, firstEventErrLine, firstEventErr)
	}
```

This preserves both boundaries: `cand == 0` (empty/header-only) and `parsed > 0` (torn row among valid rows) are **not** error states.

### 4.2 Payload surfaces the error (`derive.go`, `report.go`)

```go
// derive.go — BoardPayload
Error string `json:"error,omitempty"` // 5.7: non-empty = unparseable board, excluded from compare
```
```go
// report.go — buildFromBoard
Error: d.fatal,
```

`omitempty` keeps healthy boards byte-identical (determinism AC).

### 4.3 Zero-streak wording (`template.go`)

```js
function streakFmt(n, suffix){
  var x = (n === undefined || n === null) ? 0 : n;
  if (x <= 0) return "0 (no activity)";
  return x + "d" + (suffix || "");
}
```

Route card, board page, and compare streak renders through `streakFmt(...)`.

### 4.4 Client detail ladder (`template.go`)

Replace object/array-only `detailBody` with the full §2.4 ladder — never throws, `textContent` only:

```js
function isPlainObject(v){ return v !== null && typeof v === "object" && !Array.isArray(v); }
function trimS(s){ return String(s).replace(/^[\s\uFEFF\xA0]+/, "").replace(/[\s\uFEFF\xA0]+$/, ""); }
function parseJSONContainerStr(s){
  if (typeof s !== "string") return null;
  var t = trimS(s);
  if (!t || (t.charAt(0) !== "{" && t.charAt(0) !== "[")) return null;
  try { var v = JSON.parse(t); if (isPlainObject(v) || Array.isArray(v)) return v; } catch (e) {}
  return null;
}
function strictBase64ToJSON(s){
  if (typeof s !== "string") return null;
  var t = trimS(s); if (!t) return null; var txt = null;
  try {
    var bin = atob(t); if (!bin) return null;
    var bytes = new Uint8Array(bin.length);
    for (var i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) bytes[i] = bin.charCodeAt(i);
    if (typeof TextDecoder === "function") txt = new TextDecoder("utf-8").decode(bytes);
    else txt = decodeURIComponent(escape(bin));
  } catch (e) { return null; }
  if (txt === null) return null;
  return parseJSONContainerStr(txt);
}
function detailLadder(v){
  if (isPlainObject(v) || Array.isArray(v)) return v;   // 1
  if (typeof v === "string") {
    var p = parseJSONContainerStr(v);                   // 2
    if (p !== null) return p;
    var b = strictBase64ToJSON(v);                      // 3
    if (b !== null) return b;
  }
  return v;                                             // 4
}
function detailBody(e){
  var pre = el("pre");
  var v = e.detail;
  if (v === undefined || v === null) { pre.textContent = "(no detail)"; return pre; }
  var out;
  try { out = detailLadder(v); } catch (err) { out = v; }
  if (isPlainObject(out) || Array.isArray(out)) {
    var txt = null;
    try { txt = JSON.stringify(out, null, 2); } catch (err2) { txt = null; }
    if (txt !== null) { pre.textContent = txt; return pre; }
  }
  pre.textContent = String(out);
  return pre;
}
```

### 4.5 V11 counts panel (`template.go`)

CSS adds `.countspanel`, `.countsbox`, `.errorcard`. Board page gets a host div `#counts-panel` filled by `renderCountsPanel(bd)`; recompute from raw rows with `ComputeStats` semantics:

```js
function countsFromRaw(bd, fixtures){
  var sc = {}, pc = {};
  boardTasks(bd).forEach(function(r){
    var isFix = isFixtureRow(bd, r);
    if (!fixtures && isFix) return;
    var s = taskStatus(r); sc[s] = (sc[s] || 0) + 1;
    var p = priorityLabelOf(r); if (p !== null) pc[p] = (pc[p] || 0) + 1;
  });
  return {status: sc, priority: pc};
}
function priorityLabelOf(r){
  var v = r ? r.priority : undefined;
  if (v === undefined || v === null || v === "") return null;
  if (typeof v === "number") { if (!isFinite(v)) return null; return String(v); }
  if (typeof v === "string") return v;
  return null;
}
```

`renderCountsPanel` builds "Status composition"/"Priority composition" boxes (sorted counts, `chip(k)`), with empty states `"no tasks yet"` / `"no priorities set"`, and a fixture-count note when the toggle is on. Wire the toggle:

```js
fx.addEventListener("change", function(){ state.showFixtures = fx.checked; renderCountsPanel(bd); renderTable(bd); });
```

### 4.6 Error card + compare exclusion (`template.go`)

```js
function healthyBoards(){ return boards.filter(function(bd){ return !bd.error; }); }
```

Overview renders an error card before the normal card:

```js
    if (bd.error) {
      var ecard = el("div", "card errorcard");
      ecard.setAttribute("aria-label", "board " + bd.name + " failed to load");
      var eh = el("h2");
      eh.appendChild(el("span", null, bd.name));
      eh.appendChild(el("span", "badge", "error"));
      ecard.appendChild(eh);
      ecard.appendChild(el("div", "muted", "board data is unparseable — excluded from analytics and compare"));
      ecard.appendChild(el("pre", null, String(bd.error)));
      cards.appendChild(ecard);
      return;
    }
```

Compare uses `healthyBoards()`, lists `excluded from compare (unparseable): …`, and the `#v=compare` gate plus compare-tab visibility switch to `healthyBoards()`.

### 4.7 Regression tests

`derive_test.go`: `TestTemplateHasCountsPanel`, `TestTemplateHasDetailLadder` (also asserts old body is gone), `TestTemplateHasNoActivityStreakWording`, `TestTemplateHasErrorStateBoardCard`, `TestErrorBoardExcludedFromComparePayload`, `mustTemplateHTML`.
`load_test.go`: `TestUnparseableRequiredFileIsErrorState`, `TestUnparseableEventsFileIsErrorState`, `TestTornLineAmongValidRowsStaysWarning`, `TestEmptyAndHeaderOnlyBoardsRemainValid`.

